// A builtin is not a function value: there is no FunctionDecl to hand over, only an id the
// interpreter dispatches, so the refusal is its own message rather than a type mismatch.
//
// This pinned `len` until F217 made `len` nine `native fn` declarations. `len` now answers the
// *overload set* refusal instead ("names more than one function ... there are no arguments here to
// choose between them"), which is `generic_value_native_rejected`'s neighbour and a different
// rule. `compare` is a builtin with a single declaration, so it still reaches this one -- and as
// the builtins keep converting, the name this fixture uses will keep needing to move. That is the
// point of it: when nothing is left to put here, the message can go too.
fn main() {
    val f = compare
    print(1)
}
